          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Computing $B^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since $B^2=O,$ the matrix $B$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$",
